Cmn1=This module allows for a variety of uses.\\The main thing to remember||1
Cmn2=is the latching logic state of the module may be enabled or disabled||1
Cmn3=based on how reliably the 3rd party hardware works\\\\If you have||1
Cmn4=reliable Warmup/Cooldown delay parameters, 'Repulse' logic should||1
Cmn5=be turned off as many devices\\'Flash' OSD info when commands are||1
Cmn6=sent again.  \\\\----------------------------\\\\\\Parameter descriptions:
Cmn7=\\\\Warmup Delay: Time in seconds between when device can receive||1
Cmn8=an Input command after receiving a Power On command\\Cooldown Delay:
Cmn9=||2Time in seconds beween when device can receive a Power On command||1
Cmn10=after receiving a Power Off command.\\\\Repulse-Power:  Allows module||1
Cmn11=to reissue the currently latched power command if triggered again||1
Cmn12=by some means.\\Repulse-Input:  Allows module to reissue the currently||1
Cmn13=latched input command if triggered again.\\\\Input Triggers Power||1
Cmn14=On Command:  Allows a trigger of an input to issue a Power On command||1
Cmn15=if needed (by module's state or parameter)\\||D
Cmn16=||>If this option is enabled, selecting an input will||1
Cmn17=trigger an 'On' command press if module is in an "OFF FB" state.
Cmn18=\\                                  Allows programmer to simply||1
Cmn19=use an input press instead of an 'on' and an 'input' command for||1
Cmn20=a source trigger.\\\\Delay Beween Power/Input Repulse:  If Repulse||1
Cmn21=Power, Repulse Input AND Input Triggers Power On Command are all||1
Cmn22=enabled, this is the delay time used between reissuing the power||1
Cmn23=and input commands on an input select.\\\\
